# vfs_bind_kinds: every bind KIND on both subverbs. `vfs_bind` covers what a
# BEFORE bind at the root does to a walk; this covers the spellings themselves,
# which is what one shared reader of `instead` / `before` / `after` has to get
# right for `bindroot` and for `bind` alike.
#
# Coverage:
#   - bindroot instead / before / after, each constructing a mount dentry
#   - bind <parent> <name> instead / before / after under a walked parent
#   - string providers throughout, so the case needs no tree on disk
#
# Each line prints the id it was given. The refusal path is not scriptable --
# an unknown kind panics -- and is exercised by hand against both subverbs.
vfs register string
vfs register string
vfs bindroot 1 instead
vfs bindroot 1 before
vfs bindroot 1 after
vfs bind 0 alpha.txt 1 instead
vfs bind 0 alpha.txt 1 before
vfs bind 0 alpha.txt 1 after
